# DeepSpeed hostfile: one line per node -> "<ip> slots=<gpus-to-use>".
#
# The IPs MUST be DISTINCT, on-link addresses on a shared private network (VLAN/VPC)
# that route directly between nodes with NO 1:1 NAT in between. NCCL exchanges each
# rank's own NIC address in-band, so a NAT'd public IP or a duplicated private IP
# (the same address on every node) makes peers dial themselves -> "connection
# refused". launch_deepspeed.sh preflights this and auto-detects the NIC + master
# address from these entries, so you only edit the IPs and slots here.
#
# Replace the examples below with your cluster's real private IPs.
10.0.0.2 slots=4
10.0.0.3 slots=4
